{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1290048-the-lunar-totem-character-game","id":1290048,"title":"The Lunar totem character game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-20T12:08:04-08:00","id":1290048,"title":"The Lunar totem character game","content":"It works like this.<br /> <br /> Pick an animal, preferably one that's not so obvious (not foxes or snakes or something).<br /> <br /> The next person comes up with a short character concept for a Lunar with that Totem. Then they choose another animal.<br /> <br /> My first suggestion is my favourite animal as a child... the Meerkat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:02:42-08:00","id":1290128,"title":"","content":"The Lunar is a No Moon. Growing up in the Southeastern grasslands, they often served as lookout for the caravan they grew up on; they managed to survive the bandit attack they predicted but nobody believed, and thus Exalted. Now, they tend a swathe of villages, knowing the terrain better than it knows itself and watching with whatever pair of eyes is best for the situation. Lots of sensory, scrutiny, and territory Charms.<br /> <br /> I suggest... PELICAN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:59:17-08:00","id":1290142,"title":"","content":"Pelican Pete is a Changing Moon who has made an effort to make a name for himself at every major port in the West - just not his name. At each port he assumes the form of another sailor, pirate, or merchant, weaving tales and adding threads to the tapestry of history that are all dyed in his colors. He has a finger on the pulse of the West, and is more than happy to use his clout to spin things in the Silver Pact's favor. Lots of social charms, especially Manipulation charms, but also plenty of Intelligence charms to keep up on the various jobs he claims to have.<br /> <br /> Next: a Shrike!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","user":"Minty","date":". 02-20-2019, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:17:53-08:00","id":1290171,"title":"","content":"Wait, shrikes are real?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:31:45-08:00","id":1290181,"title":"","content":"This lunar is a Full Moon former student of Smiling Rat, known for his habit of leaving strung-up corpses of Realm soldiers in his wake. His general habit is raising an army from either local revolutionaries or a nation bordering a satrapy, and seeking to cause as much terror and destruction in a Realm satrapy until the Realm response forces him to flee. The shadowlands that often follow, as well as the amount of antipathy towards Lunars his brutal tactics can create leave the Silver Pact worried, and many Lunars hope to continue the feud with Smiling Rat by killing him.<br /> <br /> Next: Garter Snake","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:24:39-08:00","id":1290336,"title":"","content":"I had to look up garter snakes and reread the description twice because I'm Australian and the concept of &quot;harmless wildlife&quot; is foreign here. <br /> <br /> Spiraling Blossom is an androgynous beauty and long-time favourite companion of the local nobility and merchant princes. Their high-class, glamorous lifestyle is a far cry from the gutter they almost died in before Luna found them and whispered that their beauty was a weapon sharper than any knife and more potent than any venom, their words stronger tools than anything forged of steel. Spiraling Blossom did not kill the client who had beaten and left them for dead. That man's business partner did, three weeks later, after the Lunar's sibilant influence worked its way into his heart. When the Silver Pact found them, they found the Changing Moon caste to be the only natural choice. Now they coil around the heart of power in the city, their influence sinuously winding through teahouses, bordellos, council chambers, and the houses of the mighty. With a word, a look, or a lingering scent of perfume, they sculpt their society with the precision of a master artisan. When they're done, it will be something beautiful. If they can avoid getting caught up in the power plays for long enough to remember why they're doing this and who they're trying to save. <br /> <br /> Obviously lots of Appearance and Manipulation Charms, especially pheromoney ones, since that seems to be a garter snake trick. <br /> <br /> I choose a Numbat because now I want you all to have to look up something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:31:09-08:00","id":1290823,"title":"","content":"Ender of Towers is a predator of discerning tastes; his preferred prey is architects and builders. His territories are often sought as the site of hunting-lodges or other retreats by the powerful, but he will not suffer their presence. He has consumed many builders and drank their knowledge of crafting, and he wields it like a sword. When the builders start swarming, he creeps in with the face of a laborer and lurks until he can steal the face of the head architect bloodlessly. Then the game begins, using that stolen face and others to send the project into a spiral of disarray. Combined with nightly maraudings and ominous accidents, he drives the head architect to doubt their own sanity until the project is abandoned. Some he allows to leave broken; some go missing and are never found again. Later, he uses his stolen knowledge of crafts to undo the worksite's scar on his land as much as possible.<br /> <br /> A scion of house Mnemon has heard the rumors, but she is undeterred---in fact, she wants the work-ruining phantom to come to her and her sworn kin. She plans to erect a monument to his defeat, be he god, demon, or even Anathema.<br /> <br /> Probably Intelligence and Perception, with Dexterity for sneakitude as well.<br /> <br /> \u200bNext animal is... A CUTTLEFISH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:35:34-08:00","id":1291994,"title":"","content":"Shifting Veil is a changing moon native to the west, a dancer by appearance, and a thief and a spy by trade. She is known in every port along the western coasts of creation, but no two places know her by the same name. She's ever-changing, whether to meld seemlessly into the crowd, or to make a breathtaking performance that captivates the audience, allowing her companions to perform their tasks uninterrupted.<br /> <br /> Next animal is... ZEBRA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}